course: dictionary
lesson: 4752
title: Hot: many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Hot is a small word with several meanings. To find the right one, read the words around it, because they are its context and they give clues. Ask: which meaning fits this sentence?
explain: The main meaning is high temperature, as in «Vent water can be hotter than three hundred degrees.» That is far warmer than a cup of tea, so hot means very warm.
explain: Hot can also mean spicy, as in hot sauce, or feeling too warm, as in «I'm hot.» In informal talk, hot can mean very popular or new, as in the hot toy this year.
fact: Hot means having a high temperature; very warm.
fact: «An open oven door and the inside of the oven are hot enough to burn skin instantly.» Hot things can burn you, so never touch them.
fact: Heat moves from hotter things to colder things.
fact: Hot can mean spicy, as in hot sauce, which makes your mouth burn.
fact: In informal talk, hot can mean very popular or new, as in the hot toy this year.
exercise: «The hottest stars are blue-white.» In this sentence, what does hot mean? | Making your mouth burn | *Having a high temperature | Cold and wet | Very popular
exercise: Ella says hot sauce is too warm to eat. What does hot mean in hot sauce? | Very popular | *Making your mouth burn because of spices | Feeling too warm | Having a high temperature
exercise: Find and copy the word from «Vent water can be hotter than three hundred degrees» that means more heat than something else. | three | water | *hotter | degrees
test: Sam says «I'm hot» after running in the sun. What does hot mean here? | Cold and wet | Very popular | *Feeling too warm | Making your mouth burn
test: «Never touch things that might be hot» is a safety rule. Why is it important? | Hot things are slippery | Hot things are cold inside | *Hot things can burn your skin | Hot things are always popular
exam: What does hot mean in «the hot toy this year»? | Feeling too warm | *Very popular or new | Having a high temperature | Making your mouth burn
